  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🦸 Superhero Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Hero names in the shapes comics have used for ninety years."
    },
    "intro": "Superhero names follow a handful of shapes that comics have used since the 1930s: an adjective and a noun (Green Lantern), something-Man or -Woman (Spider-Man, Wonder Woman), a title (Captain America, Doctor Strange) or one bold word (Storm). This **superhero name generator** builds names in all of them, avoiding the famous ones.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The classic shapes",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Something-Man or -Woman:</strong> Superman, Batman, Spider-Man, Wonder Woman. The power or theme, then who they are.</li><li><strong>Adjective and noun:</strong> Green Lantern, Black Panther, Scarlet Witch.</li><li><strong>A title:</strong> Captain America, Doctor Strange, Mister Fantastic, Ms. Marvel. A title adds authority or a hint of the person's job.</li><li><strong>One word:</strong> Storm, Cyclops, Rogue. Short and easy to shout.</li><li><strong>The and a noun:</strong> The Flash, The Atom.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Making your hero's name work",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Say what they do,</strong> or what they stand for. A name that hints at the power saves an explanation.</li><li><strong>Check it isn't taken.</strong> The big comic publishers have used thousands of names; search before you fall in love with one, especially if you're publishing.</li><li><strong>Think about the real name too.</strong> Comics love alliteration: Peter Parker, Bruce Banner, Wally West.</li></ul><p>Every hero needs someone to fight: try the <a href=\"villain-name-generator.html\">Villain Name Generator</a>.</p><p>Putting a team together? The <a href=\"superhero-team-name-generator.html\">Superhero Team Name Generator</a> names hero alliances and secret agencies, and every hero needs a <a href=\"sidekick-name-generator.html\">sidekick</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do I come up with a superhero name?",
        "answer": "Start from the power or the theme, then pick a shape: something-Man or -Woman, an adjective and a noun, a title like Captain, or one bold word."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I use these names in my comic or game?",
        "answer": "Yes, free and with no credit needed. Check the name isn't already used by a published character first, especially for anything you sell."
